Smoke test works. Note local mode with data dir under /tmp allowed; okay. Config only rejects temp for private.

Now let's review requirements systematically and see gaps.

1. "Add an explicit deployment/runtime mode to configuration and health responses." Done. Health mode. Config.
2. "Display a mode badge and capabilities so users know whether repository execution, live OpenCode, persistence, and provider configuration are available." Done via badge/setup panel. Badge label; capabilities in setup. Maybe capabilities not always visible unless setup open. The requirement could imply a visible capabilities summary. Setup panel is accessible via button; acceptable. Maybe add a compact capability strip always visible? The mode bar summary only. To be safe, we could add a small capabilities line in mode bar showing e.g. "Repository: yes · OpenCode: live · Persistence: disk · Providers: OpenCode". But that might be noisy. The setup panel is a mode selection/setup page. The task says "Display a mode badge and capabilities". Better to make capabilities visible in the mode bar itself, perhaps with small labels. Let's add a compact capability summary in the mode bar: `<span className="mode-capabilities">Repo: selected · OpenCode: live · Storage: local · Providers: OpenCode</span>`. Could derive from capabilities. That would satisfy more directly. We can add `CapabilitySummary` component with short labels. But the mode bar already has summary and button. Add maybe below summary:
```tsx
{runtime ? <span className="mode-capabilities" aria-label="Mode capabilities">{runtime.descriptor.capabilities.filter(c=>["repository","opencode","persistence","providers"].includes(c.id)).map(c=>`${shortLabel(c.id)}: ${c.available ? "yes" : "no"}`).join(" · ")}</span> : null}
